The command line of a nixos-forge flake: built-in commands, and the forge-<name> commands a fork adds

Usage: forge <COMMAND>

Commands:
  check-docs    Check the docs: links and anchors, the docs/README.md index, names a fork lacks, a section per module
  doctor        Check this machine, one line per check: OK, WARN, FAIL or SKIP when it does not apply; run it with sudo for the checks that need root
  auto-upgrade  Pull the version CI validated for this machine and apply it, as the auto-upgrade service does
  update        Pull the host's flake checkout, then run nh os switch with the given arguments
  enroll        Enroll a TPM2 or a security key to unlock the LUKS disk of this host
  install       Install this installer's host on a whole disk, or beside Windows, asking for every value not given
  dual-boot     Keep Windows in the boot menu and the firmware boot order, or make room for NixOS beside it
  upstream      Show what the starter changed, then merge its latest release into a branch of origin and open its pull request
  init          Make a fresh fork yours: write its host and person from the examples, then remove them
  help          Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
  -h, --help     Print help
  -V, --version  Print version

External commands: none; a forge-<name> program in FORGE_COMMANDS_PATH or PATH runs as `forge <name>`.
